10531_u77b1_float_field_pyval_self_eq_strict_false.py	REFUSAL	[ir-semantic]: 'f' line 23: `d['a'] == d['a']` compares a PyVal value with a non-literal operand under `--strict-float-finite`: a PyVal float is a Why3 real in the value model (`hval_eq` / `hreal_eq` are reflexive), so a NaN is not modelled and the FLOAT-FINITE assumption this flag drops would still be relied on (route #606; CPython: `v == v` is False for v = float("nan")). Compare the PyVal value with a literal instead, or drop `--strict-float-finite`.
10533_u77c15_receiver_class_param_own_method_writes_false.py	REFUSAL	PYCSL-FUNCTION-FRAME: the function `f` declares `#@ assigns` but its body may write the parameter(s) `r` (a store rooted at it, an in-place mutator, or forwarding it to a callee that writes it), which the declared frame does not name. A caller in another module reads the declared frame, so it would assume the argument UNCHANGED across the call (route #634). Add the written location to the frame (`#@ assigns r.<field>` / `r[..]`), or stop writing it.
